# Spry and Mighty: X is the difference between the chosen creatures' powers as the spell resolves, a negative power counting as it is
# (CR 107.1b), not as it was when the spell was cast. Bot1 controls an Ornithopter (0/2) and an Elvish Mystic (1/1); with Spry and
# Mighty on the stack Bot2 Locust Sprays the Ornithopter (-1/1). With only two creatures there is nothing to choose among, so
# Bot1 is not asked: X is 1 - (-1) = 2, Bot1 draws two cards, the Ornithopter becomes 1/3 and the Mystic 3/3. (A power clamped to
# 0 would make X 1.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Gleemox
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Elvish Mystic
Ornithopter
Spry and Mighty
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Locust Spray
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Gleemox.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Gleemox.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spry and Mighty.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Locust Spray.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = -1
! Bot1.Choose
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Toughness = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 3
